version: "2.0"
name: gnomon-kernel-trace
description: >-
  Per-project trace capture: mode.ts holds the on/off state per project folder
  and capture.ts writes a traced session to its jsonl file.
context:
  - >-
    Split out of packages/gnomon/.purpose (2026-10-27); path: values stay
    relative to packages/gnomon, the package root.
components:
  trace-capture:
    description: >-
      #trace-capture (src/kernel/trace/): a CORE per-project audit mode, on
      every home and build (TD-2026-10-19-057, amends TD-2026-10-19-139). The
      human switches it on per project folder (mode.ts; CLI `gnomon trace
      on|off|status|path`); state lives ONLY in <home>/trace-folders.json
      (0600, keyed by realpath). The supervisor reads the mode at every
      session.open and resume for the session cwd and, when on, tees every
      stdin and stdout line plus kernel ctl notes to
      <home>/trace/<project key>/<hsid with ':' as '-'>.jsonl, one {t, dir,
      line} per LF line. Project key = slug of the folder name + '-' + 12 hex
      of sha256(realpath); project.json in the key dir records the realpath
      (a mismatch refuses trace-unsafe). NOTHING is written into the project
      tree. The session profile's gnomon-home deny covers <home>/trace,
      renames included; no project-tree deny exists for the trace (Aegis L7).
      Dirs 0700, files 0600, lstat + O_NOFOLLOW|O_NONBLOCK (+O_EXCL to create):
      a link, FIFO or device refuses trace-unsafe without hanging (Aegis M3).
      Refusals (TRACE_REFUSALS, published in gnomon-contracts
      D98_CLOSED_VALUES) are reported on session.sandbox{traced:false,
      traceRefused}; traced:true otherwise (both reserved under P8-D98). Never
      blocks a session: bounded queue, out dropped first, in/ctl evict queued
      out and have a reserve, drops counted in ctl notes. Aegis M1: per-record
      bound 64 KiB (truncated copy + hash + bytes); past the 50 MiB file bound
      a capped note, then in/ctl in full and out as skeletons; past 4x out is
      only counted. Aegis M2/L4: span redaction on the decoded value
      ([redacted:<kind>]: PEM, grt:v1:, sk-ant-, ghp_, github_pat_, AKIA,
      xox[bp]-, secret env values). Aegis L3: prior-close-unclean note on a
      resume after an unclean close; a drain flushes with a 2 s deadline.
      Residuals: prompt and tool text in the clear, readable by the user's own
      account outside Gnomon; exact-folder match only (a session in
      /proj/sub is untraced when /proj is traced, follow-up); in/ctl past the
      hard bound are unbounded; win32 has no POSIX modes (sessions refuse
      sandbox-unavailable). Zero deps: no logger; visibility is the kernel
      log row.
    path: src/kernel/trace/
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, kernel, audit, paradigm-8]
    tests:
      - test/trace-capture.test.ts
      - test/trace-session.test.ts
